
                          \cf\r1  Welcome to Hacker v4.5  \r0

                \c3Original game and programming by  \cbPatrick Baker
                    \c34.0 Remodifications by         \cbBob Maple\c7
                    \c74.5 Remodifications by     \cfJoseph Barrero

\cd\r1 Object of the game \r0\c7

 The object of Hacker is to beat the Hacker's Assoc. of America Computer
 You accomplish this by:

    \c91. \cbHacking other BBSes and computers\c1--\cband succeeding\c1.
    \c92. \cbHacking other users\c7
    \c93. \cbAnd when you're finally strong enough, hacking the HAA computer.
 \c7
 The first method, hacking other computers, is a good way to gain \cfexperience
 points\c7, which determine your ability to infultrate other users and BBSes.
 You call up another BBS, and try to destroy it with line noise, viruses, or
 just plain hacking.  BBSes you can be busy sometimes or not answer the phone.
 Finaly, if you have lousy hardware, it is possible to connect at 300 or 1200
 baud--and have to sit through the opening screen at a simulated baud rate.

 The second method, hacking other users, is another good way to get experience
 points.  Its a battle between you and another user playing, but doesnt allow
 viruses.  This is where experience points really count.

 To win the game you must beat the HAA computer.  To find the number to the
 HAA computer you must use the wardialer until you find it.

 \cd\r1 Commands used in the game \r0\c7

 The following is a list of all the commands used in the game, and what they
 do.  Most are self explanatory, and the two main menus resemble AmigaDOS's
 LIST command.

 \caCD DIAL              \c2This gets you to the terminal directory where you
                      can hack BBSes or computer.
 \caHAA                  \c2Hackers Association of America. Used to fix
                      hardware damage, hack credit cars, wardial, and more.
 \caTrans                \c2Used to send a 3 line message to another player.
 \caUser                 \c2Get a listing of other users playing Hacker.
 \caStats                \c2Look at your own personal statistics.
 \caTop                  \c2The Top-10 leading hackers
 \caEndCLI               \c2End the game (QUIT or Q works as well.)
 \caSpy                  \c2Get stats on another hacker.
 \caHackOther            \c2Fight another hacker (one on one)
 \caLast                 \c2List the last 10 user vs. user battles
 \caBank                 \c2Enter the bank.
 \caWHO                  \c2See who else is on the BBS
 \caOLM                  \c2Send another user on-line a message\cf
 \caScan                 \c2Scans the user list for plays that aren't
"Trashed"

 Pretty simple stuff.  So, get going! Rule the world of hacking!  Show
 everyone that you can't be out-hacked!

